  "headline": "Puan Maharani Addresses Speculation Over New Vice President Pick",
  "seoTitle": "Puan Maharani on New Vice President Selection",
  "metaDescription": "House Speaker Puan Maharani responds to reports on potential candidates to replace Gibran Rakabuming Raka as Vice President, citing presidential prerogative.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "House Speaker Puan Maharani stated that PDIP will not propose a candidate for the vice president position.",
    "Sufmi Dasco Ahmad is among the names frequently linked to the vacancy following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto holds the prerogative to select the new vice president, with an official announcement expected by November 25."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka, Indonesia's political landscape is focused on the selection of his successor. House Speaker Puan Maharani has publicly urged against speculation regarding potential candidates, emphasizing that the decision rests solely with President Prabowo Subianto. While names such as Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, Sugiono, and Ahmad Muzani have circulated as prospective appointees, Maharani confirmed that her party, PDIP, will not submit formal nominations, opting instead to respect the President's constitutional prerogative. Supporters of Dasco, including various academic voices, highlight his political experience and alignment with the President's policy platform as key qualifications. Reports indicate that the President is expected to submit his chosen candidate to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) soon, with an announcement potentially scheduled for November 25.",
